meta {
  name: Create a v3 itinerary
  type: http
  seq: 2
}
post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/acc/:acc_id/itineraries
  body: json
  auth: inherit
}
params:path {
  acc_id: {{accId}}
}
body:json {
  {
    "itinerary": {
      "file_id": "",
      "title": "",
      "prepared_for": ""
    }
  }
}
docs {
  Create a v3 itinerary

  Creates the itinerary on the Super Builder, with its default pages (cover, travel brief, map and days) and, optionally, its day-by-day events in the same request.

  Events carry real dates: the server derives the day slots and their order within a day, so the body never contains a day number, an index or a position, and the trip's own dates follow its first and last event — there is no trip_start_date to send.

  Only accounts whose itineraries are on the v3 builder can be written to; an account whose itineraries are still on the legacy builder answers 403 and keeps using the legacy API, whichever builder its lookbooks are on.

  `file_id` names the file the itinerary belongs to. A missing `file_id`, or one that is not a file the token can see in this account, is a 422.

  Scopes: files:write
}
